WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.269
-Our next guest is a very funny
actor and comedian

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.438
who stars in the critically
acclaimed series "Search Party."

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.540
The final season
is streaming on HBO Max.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.741
Let's take a look.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:11.811
-We would prefer a boy.
Um, a gay baby boy.

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.980
-Or even queer. A queer baby.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.084
-And, of course, we are
very open to all ethnicities.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.485
Of course.
-And religions.

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:22.855
-But it would be ideal if they
were 5'11" at the shortest

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.590
so that they could carry us up
the stairs to bed

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:25.758
when we're very elderly.

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:28.394
-And one-blue-eye-and-one-
brown-eye baby.

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:29.795
Like a husky.

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:32.331
-But it would be also good if he
could make us feel protected

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:35.402
like a dad, like a son
that feels like a dad.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:40.306
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend John Early.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:42.342
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.743
Welcome back, John.
-Thank you so much, Seth.

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:19.078
-It's great to have you here.
-Thank you so much.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:20.846
It's an honor to be here,

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:24.983
the hallowed halls of NBC.

00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:26.586
-Great.
-Yeah.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:30.256
-You --
-Do you mind if I sit like this?

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.624
-You can sit however you want.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.892
But I will say, you know,
you've been on the show before.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:33.893
You're a friend of the show.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.261
You seem a little
different to me.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.329
-What do you mean?

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:41.935
-Just the -- You just --
You just seem different to me.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:44.704
-In what way? In what way, Seth?

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:49.576
-You're, like, presenting in a
way that I'm less accustomed to.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:51.443
-It honestly could be that stuff

00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:54.580
is so tough
with my girlfriend at home.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:58.751
-Your -- Your -- You have a
girlfriend at home now?

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.119
-Yeah,
we just moved in together,

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:03.122
and I've never
shared space before.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:05.424
-So this is -- Okay,
this is a little strange --

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:08.494
-Do you have an IPA?

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:10.062
-You want an IPA now?
-Can I get an IPA?

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:11.264
Yeah, if that's cool.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.766
-See, here's what --
I feel like previously

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:14.767
when you've been on the show...

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.101
-Yeah?

00:02:16.101 --> 00:02:17.236
-...one of the things
you've talked about the most,

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:18.771
which I --
you know, I got to be honest,

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:22.342
I enjoy is how much
sexual chemistry you and I have.

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:25.678
And now -- and now you're kind
of coming out with presenting --

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.212
like, all of
a sudden, there's a girlfriend.

00:02:27.212 --> 00:02:29.115
-Right.
-Yeah.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:31.450
-I'm just -- Maybe I just seem
a little off because --

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.952
I mean, as excited as I am for

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.787
the Chiefs to be at
the Super Bowl --

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.755
-What?

00:02:36.755 --> 00:02:40.693
-As excited as I am for
the Chiefs, I'm also, like,

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.762
so pissed the Titans
didn't make it.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.797
-Okay. Well, that's --
See, now, this is --

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.065
You're giving yourself away
a little bit.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:49.334
-I might join the Marines,
as well.

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:52.605
-I don't know why you feel like
you have to do this.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.107
-I'm going to drop it.
Yeah, I was just like --

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:55.140
-Okay, good.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.242
-Yeah, I'm going to drop
the bit.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.076
I was having a lot of fun,
by the way,

00:02:58.076 --> 00:03:02.615
and I want to be clear
our chemistry was "on fleek."

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:05.584
But I just -- I couldn't --
I couldn't keep going

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:07.086
because I did want to
actually say hi.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.154
-And it was -- It was really --

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:09.354
You were very believable
that whole time.

00:03:09.354 --> 00:03:10.656
-Thank you, thank you.

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:11.957
I can't -- I wanna --
you know,

00:03:11.957 --> 00:03:17.130
I really think gay people
should play straight people.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.399
And, to be clear,
I think straight people

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:21.400
should play gay people.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.536
-Alright.
-Because it's hotter.

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:26.005
Everyone is always up
in arms about that.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:28.708
I'm like, I want to watch
Heath Ledger and Jake Gyllenhaal

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.942
go at it.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:33.045
Like, don't -- don't --
You know what I mean?

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:34.547
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Okay.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.916
-Hey, congratulations
on the show -- five seasons.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:37.950
-Thank you.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.685
-And I want to
ask a lot about it.

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:42.221
-Normally, there's an
applause right there, yeah.

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:43.756
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.694
Thank you.

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:50.429
-But I want to
specifically ask about --

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:53.933
That's John Waters in the clip.
The legend, John Waters.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.701
-The legend, my father.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:59.038
-What was it like --
How was he as a scene partner?

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.073
-Oh, my God, he is such a f--

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:02.841
I almost wanted to say
the F-word.

00:04:02.841 --> 00:04:04.811
He is such a professional.

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.246
He is just, like --
-Yeah.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:09.982
-By F-word, by the way,
I meant F-ing professional.

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:11.483
I wasn't --
-Just do it so they know.

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:14.020
-The [bleep] professional.
-There you go.

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:20.293
-There's a delay, there's a
delay, there's a delay.

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:21.694
Sorry.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:25.130
You know, I get -- I get,
you know, at 30 Rock

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.366
and then I want to --
Is Lorne watching?

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:30.202
You know, and I want to --
-Right, yeah.

00:04:30.202 --> 00:04:31.804
Oh, he does. He's the producer.
He watches everything.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.839
-He watches every night.
It's so beautiful, yeah.

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:36.241
-It's so beautiful.

00:04:36.241 --> 00:04:37.676
-No, wait, John Waters.
Oh, yeah.

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:40.880
I mean, like, he is my --
He created the sensibility that,

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.216
like, the show lives in.

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:47.286
He created my entire persona,
you know, my sense of humor.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.789
Like, so it was
very overwhelming.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:52.425
I was, like -- I was in my -- I
was, like, getting choked up

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:54.760
in my trailer imagining,
like, talking to him.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.229
And then you just get on set,
and he's just, like,

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:57.229
the most ordinary -- He's, like,

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:58.697
such a sweet guy and so boring.

00:04:58.697 --> 00:05:01.500
It's such a bad story. Go home!

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.736
This whole appearance
has sucked!

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:07.073
-But does he go --
Does he show up being, like --

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:08.407
I mean, you know,
does he show up, like,

00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:09.776
bigger than the project
or does he --

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:11.277
Like you said,
he's a professional. Like...

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:12.578
-He is such a professional.

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:15.381
He's so -- He's, like,
truly more off-book than me.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:18.684
-Yeah.
-Like, which was humiliating.

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:20.519
Like, he had, like,
these long, chunky lines,

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:23.255
and I was, like -- I was so in
awe of what he was doing.

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:27.393
And then I was
just, like, "Line."

00:05:28.293 --> 00:05:29.362
-Do you -- You know, obviously,

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.196
the scene's about
adopting a baby.

00:05:31.196 --> 00:05:34.166
Is that -- Do you want to be
a father in real life?

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:35.768
-Well, I can't.

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:38.804
-What?
-The ban.

00:05:38.804 --> 00:05:41.340
Like, gay people
can't have babies.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.676
-No, no, they can. They can now.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:45.278
-Well, they can't get married.

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:47.280
-Yeah, no, they can do both.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:54.120
-Okay, I've been kind of, like,
exploiting that oppression

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.320
for all of my career, and now...

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:56.422
-Oh.

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:58.024
-And now you're saying
the door is open?

00:05:58.024 --> 00:05:59.425
-Yeah.

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:01.994
-Okay.

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.897
How are your kids?
-They're great.

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:06.099
-Good.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.700
How does that feel?
-What?

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.404
-To be asked a question
for once in your life?

00:06:12.204 --> 00:06:14.807
I'm sorry. Sorry. I'm sorry.

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:19.178
I'm getting -- I get hostile.
I get hostile when I'm nervous.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:20.312
I lash out.

00:06:20.312 --> 00:06:23.082
-You mentioned being
in the building 30 Rock.

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:25.484
You were also --
Your first TV show.

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.920
-Yeah.
-For first TV job was "30 Rock."

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:32.591
-Yeah. It was -- I was such
a huge fan of "30 Rock."

00:06:32.591 --> 00:06:34.660
Another -- Jane Krakowski
also fully created me.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:35.894
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:06:35.894 --> 00:06:39.532
Like, I would not --
Like, I owe it all to her.

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:41.166
And my mom.

00:06:41.166 --> 00:06:43.235
Um, sorry, sorry.

00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:48.040
But, yeah, so,
I got the job to play, like,

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.176
one of her, like,
test-tube babies.

00:06:51.176 --> 00:06:53.212
-Wow.
-And I was so excited.

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:56.349
I had never done anything
on TV and I was so excited,

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:59.785
and I had like
five, maybe six lines.

00:06:59.785 --> 00:07:03.956
And I was, like --
I was so amped up and so, like,

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.591
trying to get them to notice me.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:07.959
Like, I was just, like, creating
this narrative of, like,

00:07:07.959 --> 00:07:09.996
"I'm going to go on for this,
like, day-player role,

00:07:09.996 --> 00:07:12.832
and Tina is
going to be like, 'It's him.'"

00:07:14.166 --> 00:07:16.535
And so every scene, even though
I'm like one of six

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:18.804
of her kids in this --
like, in this --

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:20.806
the conceit
of that episode, like --

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:23.209
And everyone was so
professional and, like, still

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:25.544
as she's, like, talking to
a group of six people.

00:07:25.544 --> 00:07:27.780
And it's --
So, it's like five models,

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.982
and then me over here, like...

00:07:32.017 --> 00:07:35.253
I'm, like, just -- I'm like...

00:07:35.253 --> 00:07:37.123
in every scene.

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:40.259
And then I had a full --
It was so, like,

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:42.027
life-changing to be on that set.

00:07:42.027 --> 00:07:46.031
And then I had,
like, a viewing party,

00:07:46.031 --> 00:07:48.701
like, with a group of friends.

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:50.169
And I was like, "Get ready.

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:52.604
Like five, maybe six lines,
but I did a lot of improv.

00:07:52.604 --> 00:07:55.441
They'll probably work that in."

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:57.809
And then everything had been cut

00:07:57.809 --> 00:07:59.745
except for one three-word line.

00:07:59.745 --> 00:08:01.780
-So, this is --
I want everybody here

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.850
to imagine they're at
John's viewing party.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:06.552
And John is expecting --
You're thinking

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:08.987
minimum five, maybe 15 lines.

00:08:08.987 --> 00:08:10.289
-Maybe -- Yeah, maybe 15.

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:12.157
And they're going to
cut to me, you know,

00:08:12.157 --> 00:08:14.560
because of all the
physical stuff I was doing.

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:15.694
-And this was
the entirety of it.

00:08:15.694 --> 00:08:16.795
Let's take a look.
-Yeah.

00:08:16.795 --> 00:08:17.930
-I didn't want to say anything

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.332
because I was trying to be
a good mother,

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:20.967
but you're cheesy,
and everyone hates you.

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:23.302
-No, Jenna, you.

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:25.338
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:28.173 --> 00:08:30.543
-I mean, I saw it.
-Thank you.

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:34.246
I mean,
it was crushing at the time,

00:08:34.246 --> 00:08:35.515
but look at me now.

00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:37.750
-Look at you now.
This is very exciting.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:41.621
First of all, congratulations.
The fifth season is fantastic.

00:08:41.621 --> 00:08:43.455
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:43.455 --> 00:08:44.957
You have to watch it.

00:08:44.957 --> 00:08:46.658
-"Search Party"
is streaming on HBO Max.

00:08:46.658 --> 00:08:47.860
And you're going to
stick around,

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.061
and Aidy Bryant
is going to come back.

00:08:49.061 --> 00:08:50.663
We'll see you right after
this commercial break.

00:08:50.663 --> 00:08:51.731
-Thank you, Seth.
[ Cheers and applause ]

